"""ABRASAX HUD v2 — borderless, always-on-top Dear ImGui overlay.

A translucent floating instrument panel that renders the live synaptic-brain
field, the runtime's vital signs, per-service dots and a chat line into the
AbrASax gateway, on top of every other window.

    python SCRIPTS/ui/abrasax_hud.py                 # config-driven start
    python SCRIPTS/ui/abrasax_hud.py --monitor 2     # top-right of monitor 2
    python SCRIPTS/ui/abrasax_hud.py --scale 1.25    # override saved/auto scale
    python SCRIPTS/ui/abrasax_hud.py --ask "status?" # chat once, at startup

Controls
    Ctrl+L    toggle click-through (WS_EX_TRANSPARENT on the GLFW HWND).
              While active the same combo is registered as a global hotkey so
              the HUD can be released even though it no longer takes mouse
              focus. Ctrl+Shift+L does the same from anywhere, always.
    Ctrl+H    hide / show (global while hidden, otherwise focused).
    Ctrl+T    toggle always-on-top.
    Enter     send the chat line.
    Esc       quit.

State
    SCRIPTS/ui/hud_config.json holds x, y, scale and click_through. It is
    written on drag-release, on a click-through toggle and on exit, and read
    on start. --monitor overrides the saved position, --scale the saved scale.

Data
    GET  :9626/state + :9626/texture (brain facade), fallback :9001/brain/*.
    POST :9001/v1/chat/completions  model lmstudio:liquid/lfm2.5-1.2b (route
         pinned: the gateway's auto route defaults to the 27B), max_tokens 256.
    LOGS/ops-state.json -> service dots (services_down first, then up).

Log
    LOGS/abrasax-hud.log gets `start`, every config/toggle event, chat results,
    any fatal exception with traceback, and `exit after N frames`.
"""
